This project is derived from Li2NegHalf (version of 2026-09-27), a Lean 4 proof
of the irrationality of Li₂(−1/2) by Qian Tang (GitHub: dtq1997), licensed under
the Apache License 2.0. Every file derived from Li2NegHalf or from the projects
listed below starts with a header naming its source and stating whether it was
modified. Files without such a header are original to this project.

Mathematical sources
  A. Fauzan, ζ(5) is irrational, preprint, Zenodo (2026),
    doi:10.5281/zenodo.22826419.
  Persiflage, zeta(5) is irrational, blog post (2026-09-24),
    https://galoisrepresentations.org/2026/09/24/zeta5-is-irrational/
  Qian Tang, A Characterization of Umbral Calculus Inspired by Fractional Sums,
    arXiv:2103.09117 (2021).

Related work (ideas only; no code from these projects is included)
  domino14/zeta5, by César Del Solar: https://github.com/domino14/zeta5
  dtq1997/li2-half-irrationality, by Qian Tang: reflective integer checking of
    certificates. https://github.com/dtq1997/li2-half-irrationality

The Lean code was written with the assistance of AI systems (OpenAI GPT-6-Astra,
Anthropic Claude Opus 5.5).

